I am personally not currently that opinionated about what Ethereuem should do with staking. just the following;

if we do nothing at all, we have the exact same issue as bitcoin: our security level will directly depend on L1 usage levels. that is bad, that means the protocol doesn't actually guarantee a minimum security level. also, this problem would play out on the order of decades, by then it will be practically impossible to change and fix the protocol

so if we do something (eventually, not super urgent), it should be a mechanism that is actually intentional about stake participation. intentional can mean 0.5%, can mean 20%, can mean 50%, can mean 100%. whatever we end up wanting to do.

